WEBVTT

00:00.501 --> 00:04.963
I need to know the truth
about Hijikata Toshizo.

00:05.088 --> 00:09.218
He had the same look in his eyes as you.

00:09.718 --> 00:13.639
What's the fun
in doing the sensible thing?

00:13.764 --> 00:17.851
Doing what no one else
can is what makes you a badass.

00:18.435 --> 00:19.853
It was the final years of Edo.

00:22.314 --> 00:26.693
There were men who lived fiercely
and passionately by the way of the sword.

00:27.236 --> 00:30.197
To become the strongest man there is.

00:30.322 --> 00:33.450
What a coincidence. Same here.

00:36.286 --> 00:41.708
I welcome you as the fools who are ready
to die alongside the Aizu!

00:43.001 --> 00:46.255
They pressed on with unwavering resolve
against the tide of history.

00:50.759 --> 00:53.220
This is the story of the last samurai

00:54.388 --> 01:00.435
men who bloomed brilliantly
in an age of turmoil, and then fell.

01:01.186 --> 01:02.896
Let us bloom with all our might.

01:07.276 --> 01:13.198
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

01:13.323 --> 01:18.370
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

01:23.667 --> 01:29.047
APRIL 1862, TOSA

01:34.928 --> 01:36.972
Man, Edo is amazing!

01:38.848 --> 01:41.226
It was packed with people,
and the food was delicious.

01:41.351 --> 01:44.229
And, what's more, there were
a ton of strong fighters, too.

01:44.813 --> 01:49.109
But Toshi was
the strongest out of them all.

01:49.401 --> 01:52.988
You just told us that story about Toshi.
That's the fifth time.

01:54.656 --> 01:57.075
Is that true, Ukichi?

01:57.200 --> 02:01.246
But still, Izo, since it makes you laugh

02:01.371 --> 02:03.582
I'd be happy to hear it five or six times!

02:03.707 --> 02:05.208
Hey!

02:06.376 --> 02:10.589
Never mind all that.
Did you get a taste of this?

02:12.507 --> 02:15.177
What? Do you eat pinkies?

02:15.302 --> 02:19.890
You idiot! Edo has Yoshiwara,
the land's greatest pleasure district!

02:20.015 --> 02:24.436
I'm talking about women!

02:24.561 --> 02:29.274
I'm... not very good with women.

02:29.399 --> 02:32.486
I've never seen or "tasted"
anything like that.

02:37.866 --> 02:41.411
Hey, Izo!
Master Takechi is calling for you!

02:45.791 --> 02:47.084
Assassination?

02:47.918 --> 02:49.336
Keep your voice down, Izo.

02:50.337 --> 02:52.381
But still, an assassination...

02:54.132 --> 02:56.301
It's divine retribution, Izo.

02:57.427 --> 02:58.595
Divine retribution?

02:59.805 --> 03:02.099
We are to eliminate Yoshida Toyo.

03:04.476 --> 03:05.602
Who is that?

03:06.895 --> 03:08.980
You don't even know who Toyo is?

03:09.398 --> 03:12.734
He's the ringleader in Tosa
who oppresses lower-class samurai like us.

03:13.443 --> 03:16.154
He sides with the shogunate's plan
to open the country

03:16.738 --> 03:19.783
a vile man who is leading
our nation to ruin.

03:21.368 --> 03:22.369
Izo.

03:23.453 --> 03:26.707
You, too, are a member
of the Tosa Loyalist Party.

03:30.001 --> 03:31.461
Lend me your strength

03:32.796 --> 03:34.381
to restore the emperor
and expel the foreigners.

03:51.898 --> 03:55.485
No, I can't do that. Anything but that.

03:55.610 --> 03:57.279
Izo!

03:57.404 --> 03:59.531
You would really turn down Master Takechi?

04:00.449 --> 04:03.660
But I don't like killing people.

04:04.953 --> 04:05.996
I'm sorry.

04:07.789 --> 04:09.666
- Hey! Get back here, Izo!
- Wait, Izo!

04:09.791 --> 04:11.585
- Let him go.
- But, Master Takechi...

04:12.419 --> 04:14.629
Well, wait and see.

04:25.307 --> 04:26.975
Why would anyone do this?

04:30.270 --> 04:31.813
Ukichi!

04:36.818 --> 04:38.236
Ukichi!

04:42.824 --> 04:44.409
Ukichi.

04:44.534 --> 04:45.619
Ukichi.

04:46.787 --> 04:48.747
They were making an example
of Ukichi's father!

04:50.207 --> 04:53.585
He petitioned the domain
to lessen the burden of the labor tax.

04:56.171 --> 04:57.506
And the one who gave the order

04:59.424 --> 05:00.634
had to be Yoshida Toyo.

05:03.512 --> 05:04.763
That damn Toyo!

05:05.305 --> 05:07.849
How much more will he make us suffer?

05:41.174 --> 05:42.551
Ukichi.

05:45.971 --> 05:47.180
Ukichi.

06:02.529 --> 06:03.572
I...

06:07.659 --> 06:09.244
will avenge...

06:13.081 --> 06:14.374
you.

06:19.629 --> 06:21.298
I'm sorry, Ukichi.

06:24.342 --> 06:25.719
I'm sorry, Izo.

06:46.615 --> 06:48.658
Yoshida Toyo, this is divine retribution!

07:00.795 --> 07:03.506
Do you think a bunch
of Loyalist Party monkeys

07:05.008 --> 07:06.885
can take me down?

07:14.225 --> 07:15.310
Why?

07:17.729 --> 07:18.939
Why...

07:20.649 --> 07:22.859
Why did you kill Ukichi?

07:24.027 --> 07:25.946
Another one, huh?

07:27.614 --> 07:28.740
Ukichi...

07:31.117 --> 07:33.995
looked up to me like an older brother.

07:34.996 --> 07:37.624
What is this nonsense you're spouting?

07:38.707 --> 07:41.419
You die first!

07:48.677 --> 07:51.054
Impossible that a lowly samurai...

07:53.723 --> 07:57.102
could be this skilled...

08:00.772 --> 08:01.940
Izo!

08:02.691 --> 08:04.067
You did it!

08:04.317 --> 08:07.112
It's divine retribution!

08:07.654 --> 08:08.947
You did it, Izo!

08:18.707 --> 08:20.750
And that was the beginning
of Izo the Manslayer.

08:22.836 --> 08:28.633
After that,
following Takechi Hanpeita's orders

08:29.426 --> 08:31.720
he cut down one key shogunate official
after another.

08:35.265 --> 08:36.683
So he was

08:37.225 --> 08:41.187
a completely different man from when
he met my grandfather, Hijikata Toshizo.

08:41.770 --> 08:46.276
A different man? That's putting it mildly.

08:48.403 --> 08:52.574
When a man with a kind soul
is forced to keep killing brutally

08:52.699 --> 08:55.785
do you know what happens to him?

09:01.791 --> 09:03.418
He shatters.

09:04.502 --> 09:05.920
Hold it!

09:06.046 --> 09:07.130
KYO, ONE YEAR LATER

09:08.131 --> 09:10.175
Surrender, Izo the Manslayer!

09:11.843 --> 09:12.927
Stay away.

09:15.138 --> 09:16.514
Don't come near.

10:23.957 --> 10:25.875
Hey... Hey!

10:26.000 --> 10:27.669
Hey, what's going on?

10:27.919 --> 10:28.920
The Mibu Ronin are coming.

10:29.045 --> 10:30.880
The Mibu Roshigumi?

10:31.005 --> 10:34.801
Check out that cocky bastard strutting
at the very front.

10:34.926 --> 10:37.679
Rumor is he killed Tanaka Shinbei.

10:37.887 --> 10:40.306
- Hijikata Toshizo, the vice-commander?
- Yes.

10:40.974 --> 10:42.350
Toshizo?

10:46.020 --> 10:47.856
- Hey, they're coming.
- Yeah.

11:28.229 --> 11:29.606
What's up, Toshi?

11:31.232 --> 11:33.568
I feel like we're being watched.

11:35.111 --> 11:36.571
A loyalist assassin?

11:39.032 --> 11:40.950
No, it's probably nothing.

12:06.935 --> 12:10.355
By this time, the Mibu Roshigumi had grown

12:10.813 --> 12:13.983
and was split into two major factions.

12:15.526 --> 12:18.571
The first was led
by Commander Kondo Isami...

12:18.696 --> 12:19.864
One!

12:19.989 --> 12:25.078
...with Vice-Commanders Hijikata Toshizo
and Yamanami Keisuke

12:25.536 --> 12:27.288
the Shieikan faction.

12:28.081 --> 12:30.917
- One, two!
- One, two!

12:31.042 --> 12:35.463
- One, two!
- One, two!

12:36.089 --> 12:39.717
The other was the Serizawa faction,
led by First Commander Serizawa Kamo

12:40.551 --> 12:42.971
Vice-Commander Niimi Nishiki

12:43.930 --> 12:49.936
and Assistant Vice-Commander
Hirayama Goro.

12:51.271 --> 12:52.897
Don't tell me

12:53.940 --> 12:59.696
they went out drinking again
last night and still aren't back.

13:01.698 --> 13:04.993
Those bastards!

13:05.118 --> 13:06.953
Incredible!

13:07.078 --> 13:09.038
Mr. Todo sure is impressive!

13:09.163 --> 13:11.207
How about that, Shimada?

13:13.084 --> 13:15.962
SHIMADA KAI

13:16.087 --> 13:17.964
Damn, Shimada!

13:18.089 --> 13:19.090
Like a god of war!

13:19.215 --> 13:23.428
Hey, Shimada! Don't get cocky, rookie!

13:24.012 --> 13:25.930
I'm sorry. I got a little carried away.

13:26.055 --> 13:29.475
Put those down, now! Put those down!

13:29.726 --> 13:31.978
All of you, drop and give me push-ups!

13:33.521 --> 13:34.564
Mr. Yamanami.

13:41.571 --> 13:47.702
- 11, 12, 13
- 11, 12, 13

13:47.827 --> 13:54.792
- 14, 15, 16...
- 14, 15, 16...

14:00.798 --> 14:02.467
You want to switch to the other faction?

14:05.720 --> 14:06.804
Tell me why.

14:08.097 --> 14:11.184
I wish to train under Master Serizawa.

14:12.143 --> 14:15.688
They see more action,
and they're flush with cash.

14:16.147 --> 14:19.233
Plus, it's fun.
They get to party almost every night.

14:20.109 --> 14:21.486
- Exactly.
- Exactly.

14:23.154 --> 14:24.530
So that's the real reason, huh?

14:31.662 --> 14:32.997
Well, yeah. That makes sense.

14:36.584 --> 14:37.752
Fine.

14:38.836 --> 14:39.837
Do whatever you want.

14:41.339 --> 14:42.382
Are you serious?

14:42.507 --> 14:44.675
Yeah, but..

14:45.551 --> 14:47.136
on one condition.

14:49.430 --> 14:50.807
Wake up, Gen!

14:52.350 --> 14:53.643
It's starting again!

14:57.188 --> 14:58.439
Yes.

14:59.690 --> 15:03.528
Well, look who's all here.

15:04.195 --> 15:06.572
Hey, it hasn't started yet, right?

15:06.697 --> 15:07.907
It starts now.

15:08.199 --> 15:09.409
Hey

15:10.159 --> 15:11.411
come at me all at once.

15:13.246 --> 15:15.164
If you can land just one strike on me

15:16.165 --> 15:18.668
you can go to Serizawa's group
or wherever the hell you want.

15:18.793 --> 15:19.794
Awesome.

15:19.919 --> 15:21.504
Not confident, even four against one?

15:21.838 --> 15:24.340
If you're that pathetic,
they won't give you the time of day.

15:27.051 --> 15:30.096
Hijikata, mind if we add three more?

15:30.221 --> 15:31.514
Yeah, I don't care.

15:32.265 --> 15:33.266
That's seven men!

15:33.391 --> 15:35.518
But even for Mr. Hijikata, that's...

15:39.188 --> 15:40.231
Hey.

15:41.274 --> 15:44.110
- On guard!
- C'mon, take it seriously!

15:44.235 --> 15:46.112
What are you, scared? Hey!

15:46.237 --> 15:48.364
- There are seven of us! We can win this!
- Yeah!

15:48.489 --> 15:50.616
- Good luck.
- Yeah.

15:53.411 --> 15:56.164
Get him!

16:03.713 --> 16:06.340
What's the matter? Bring it!

16:13.181 --> 16:14.182
Hey.

16:16.267 --> 16:17.435
So, I take it you're all staying?

16:19.395 --> 16:22.690
Whoa! Look at you go, Toshi!

16:24.317 --> 16:28.905
That was pathetic, you guys. Gen.

16:30.615 --> 16:31.699
What is this?

16:33.284 --> 16:34.285
Hey!

16:34.410 --> 16:35.703
I'll assist you.

16:38.331 --> 16:40.249
So it's against you two?

16:43.002 --> 16:45.338
Now this is getting interesting.

17:16.368 --> 17:17.369
Dammit!

17:17.494 --> 17:18.746
Hey, it's not a lethal blow.

17:18.871 --> 17:20.289
Awesome!

17:20.414 --> 17:22.458
Damn. He got me!

17:22.875 --> 17:25.545
Man, what were you thinking?

17:25.670 --> 17:28.589
What's the matter?
Are you that pissed you lost to me?

17:28.756 --> 17:32.885
That's not it! You won the fight
against those guys, didn't you?

17:33.010 --> 17:35.221
So why did you run them all off?

17:35.346 --> 17:37.974
If they want to leave,
there's no use trying to stop them.

17:39.433 --> 17:41.102
That's so like you, Toshi.

17:41.352 --> 17:43.563
There you go again, being so nonchalant.

17:43.688 --> 17:47.400
Do you know how many men
we've lost to them this month?

17:47.525 --> 17:49.026
Pardon the intrusion.

17:51.320 --> 17:53.614
You must all be tired.
Please help yourselves.

17:54.782 --> 17:56.534
Perfect timing.

17:57.243 --> 17:58.661
You're always so thoughtful, Aijiro.

17:58.911 --> 18:02.290
Not at all. I'm honored
you remembered my name, sir.

18:03.249 --> 18:06.669
What are you so tense about?

18:06.794 --> 18:10.298
He's never this well-behaved around me.

18:10.423 --> 18:13.759
Even in the last practice,
he mercilessly beat me down.

18:13.884 --> 18:15.136
That's not right.

18:15.261 --> 18:17.305
The one always beating me down
is you, Master!

18:17.430 --> 18:19.890
See? He's usually got
a much bigger mouth on him.

18:20.016 --> 18:23.477
What's this?
Bragging about your cute little disciple?

18:30.359 --> 18:31.694
But

18:31.819 --> 18:33.446
is this really okay?

18:34.405 --> 18:36.824
For someone like me,
the son of a craftsman

18:37.950 --> 18:39.952
to join the Mibu Roshigumi?

18:42.455 --> 18:44.457
If you can't join our ranks

18:45.124 --> 18:46.917
then we'd all have to quit on the spot.

18:47.960 --> 18:49.086
Right, Toshi?

18:50.755 --> 18:52.923
We're just farm boys ourselves.

18:54.842 --> 18:55.843
Aijiro...

18:57.386 --> 18:58.638
being a samurai isn't
about your social status.

19:00.389 --> 19:01.557
It's about what's in here.

19:06.437 --> 19:09.065
Commander Kondo, everyone...

19:09.190 --> 19:13.944
I swear I'll make myself useful
to all of you!

19:15.446 --> 19:17.406
Good. See that you do, Kojiro.

19:18.157 --> 19:19.867
- It's Aijiro.
- Yeah, I know.

19:21.035 --> 19:22.370
Thank you.

19:25.539 --> 19:28.209
Man, that's something else.

19:30.461 --> 19:33.673
That master-disciple bond, you know?
It gets you right here.

19:33.798 --> 19:36.884
Seriously, I'm so damn jealous.

19:37.593 --> 19:39.136
I want one of those, too.

19:39.470 --> 19:40.930
What the hell do you want?

19:42.431 --> 19:43.808
Hey, Saeki!

19:43.933 --> 19:46.143
What are you doing skulking around here?

19:46.268 --> 19:49.689
What about your patrol?
You're supposed to be on duty today!

19:50.898 --> 19:52.149
Oh, that's right.

19:52.316 --> 19:54.360
SAEKI MATASABURO

19:54.485 --> 19:56.904
I heard he was out again last night.

19:57.655 --> 19:59.990
You know, what's-his-name.

20:00.116 --> 20:03.327
What was it again? Uzo? Muzo?

20:06.163 --> 20:09.959
Izo! That's it, Izo. Okada Izo.

20:11.794 --> 20:14.505
He was prowling Tominokoji last night.

20:15.548 --> 20:16.799
Tominokoji?

20:19.427 --> 20:21.053
You can just leave him to me.

20:22.346 --> 20:24.682
If you don't dispose of thugs
like him quickly

20:24.807 --> 20:27.017
a man can't enjoy his sake in peace.

20:27.560 --> 20:29.478
Are you trying to pick a fight?

20:30.479 --> 20:32.022
What's that supposed to mean?

20:32.857 --> 20:34.859
Okada Izo is a manslayer, you know.

20:37.570 --> 20:40.656
Or is he a "friend" of yours,
Vice-Commander?

20:41.157 --> 20:44.952
In fact, isn't protecting him the same
as picking a fight with our Aizu patrons?

20:47.913 --> 20:50.040
Saeki isn't wrong about any of this.

20:50.166 --> 20:51.459
This isn't right, Toshi.

20:51.584 --> 20:52.710
Saeki.

20:54.044 --> 20:55.546
I apologize for the trouble.

20:57.256 --> 21:01.051
But Toshi would never do anything
to endanger the corps.

21:01.177 --> 21:02.303
You can count on that.

21:04.513 --> 21:09.393
I need you to give it your all
as a Vice-Commander's Assistant.

21:12.563 --> 21:14.732
Well, I can't exactly say no
to the commander, can I?

21:15.107 --> 21:16.942
Well, then, I'll be off on my patrol.

21:31.582 --> 21:35.002
Boss! Why is he the same rank as me?

21:35.127 --> 21:36.212
Settle down.

21:37.630 --> 21:39.632
Saeki's attitude isn't something
to be proud of.

21:40.674 --> 21:43.594
But you've noticed it as well, I'm sure.

21:45.638 --> 21:47.598
His killing intent is not
to be taken lightly.

21:48.182 --> 21:52.019
We'll likely see more men of his ilk
joining our ranks from now on.

21:52.728 --> 21:55.689
Yeah, we're getting more and more guys
with murky pasts.

21:56.649 --> 21:59.610
It's increasingly difficult
to maintain control.

22:02.696 --> 22:04.949
We may need to take some measures.

22:35.729 --> 22:39.608
Looks like the master of this place
has agreed to our "donation."

22:53.747 --> 22:55.082
Come on, have a drink.

22:55.207 --> 22:59.712
Master Serizawa,
you should train us sometime.

22:59.837 --> 23:03.924
It's always booze and women with you.
Our enemies will walk all over us.

23:07.303 --> 23:10.598
Oume, go ahead and train him.

23:10.723 --> 23:13.851
- Me? Are you sure?
- Yeah.

23:14.852 --> 23:16.061
Are you...

23:17.563 --> 23:18.939
really that strong?

23:20.274 --> 23:21.650
You're always drunk off your ass.

23:23.110 --> 23:24.570
I bet even I could take you.

23:26.697 --> 23:31.160
I may not look it, but I've cut down
a Hokushin Itto-ryu master, too.

23:32.786 --> 23:35.247
Is that right? Heh.

23:36.040 --> 23:39.209
All right, I like your nerve.
I'll give you a lesson.

23:42.755 --> 23:45.257
Try to kill me. Right now.

23:46.967 --> 23:48.260
Hell, if anything

23:49.386 --> 23:51.472
I'll even fight you bare-handed.

23:53.891 --> 23:56.143
I'm the chief commander of the Mibu Ronin.

23:56.268 --> 23:58.729
If you take me down,
you'll be famous overnight.

23:58.854 --> 24:02.149
The Imperialists might pay you a fortune.

24:02.608 --> 24:03.776
Or perhaps...

24:07.613 --> 24:11.742
are you afraid of me,
even when I'm unarmed?

24:19.792 --> 24:20.918
Don't you mock me.

24:26.090 --> 24:27.091
Come on.

24:32.638 --> 24:36.684
Hey, do you all get it now?
This is how I train.

24:37.351 --> 24:39.770
Come try to kill me
whenever you want. Got it?

24:45.401 --> 24:47.695
I'll follow your lead, Serizawa!

24:47.820 --> 24:49.863
Pour it over my hand.

25:04.837 --> 25:07.131
You're pretty damn good.

25:08.007 --> 25:09.842
You've got some skills yourself.

25:12.553 --> 25:15.431
We'll have another match, Toshizo.

25:16.348 --> 25:17.433
Sure.

25:23.897 --> 25:27.818
You. What are you doing here?

25:35.159 --> 25:36.285
You're...

25:37.870 --> 25:39.079
Okada Izo.

25:39.580 --> 25:40.664
Izo?

25:44.960 --> 25:46.462
Don't come.

25:49.673 --> 25:51.008
You mustn't come.

25:54.887 --> 25:56.013
Don't come.

25:59.391 --> 26:01.018
You mustn't come.

26:12.905 --> 26:14.198
Again.

26:23.624 --> 26:25.000
A manslayer...

26:27.002 --> 26:28.295
A manslayer like me...

26:33.717 --> 26:34.885
has no right...

26:38.430 --> 26:40.057
to show up

26:41.183 --> 26:42.392
before Toshizo.

26:57.449 --> 27:00.994
I guess it was after you all passed by.

27:01.829 --> 27:03.872
He was rummaging through scraps

27:03.997 --> 27:07.084
and other trash for food to eat.

27:07.209 --> 27:08.794
Eating trash?

27:08.919 --> 27:13.715
Yeah. It was a ghastly sight to see.

27:20.389 --> 27:21.974
It was right here.

27:51.003 --> 27:53.172
Will you let me know if you see him again?

27:57.050 --> 27:59.011
Before the magistrate's office.

28:01.388 --> 28:02.472
Got it?

28:03.098 --> 28:04.349
Understood.

28:08.061 --> 28:09.313
It's the manslayer again!

28:09.438 --> 28:13.150
Move out of my way!

28:18.155 --> 28:19.907
Hey, go on home now!

28:20.032 --> 28:21.033
What happened?

28:24.119 --> 28:25.704
Go home now.

28:27.164 --> 28:28.540
Go home!

28:38.425 --> 28:39.468
Toshi.

28:49.394 --> 28:51.021
They both went down with a single strike.

28:53.065 --> 28:55.484
As far as I know,
there is only one person capable

28:57.069 --> 28:58.278
of a feat like this.

29:01.615 --> 29:02.658
It's Izo.

29:06.203 --> 29:08.038
I have to find him, and fast.

29:09.623 --> 29:10.666
Do you have any leads?

29:11.124 --> 29:12.167
No.

29:12.834 --> 29:14.336
But he has to be close.

29:16.838 --> 29:18.215
What will you do when you find him?

29:27.099 --> 29:28.100
Cut him down.

29:33.146 --> 29:34.439
Are you really sure about that?

29:37.276 --> 29:42.030
If you fight Izo with a heartless blade,
you'll be no different than a manslayer.

29:42.155 --> 29:44.992
If I don't do this now,
more people will die.

29:45.117 --> 29:46.535
That won't do for you two!

29:50.122 --> 29:51.206
That won't do.

29:58.630 --> 30:02.134
Did you two meet just to kill each other?

30:04.428 --> 30:05.429
Remember...

30:08.473 --> 30:10.183
why you aimed to be the strongest.

30:14.980 --> 30:16.315
You two were...

30:21.236 --> 30:22.404
friends.

30:24.197 --> 30:25.282
Right?

30:31.246 --> 30:32.456
Before I'm his friend

30:34.624 --> 30:36.501
I'm the vice-commander
of the Mibu Roshigumi.

30:53.185 --> 30:54.311
Izo.

31:27.010 --> 31:28.178
I've been looking for you...

31:29.513 --> 31:30.555
Izo.

31:44.653 --> 31:45.695
Toshizo.

31:50.283 --> 31:51.368
Hey.

31:55.247 --> 31:56.498
It's been a while.

32:02.337 --> 32:03.338
Toshizo.

32:10.595 --> 32:11.638
What is it?

32:16.768 --> 32:17.769
I'm...

32:20.689 --> 32:21.731
I'm...

32:25.402 --> 32:27.737
I kept cutting down people on command.

32:30.323 --> 32:31.408
And the men I fought

32:34.286 --> 32:35.871
started to look like scarecrows.

32:39.708 --> 32:40.750
Now

32:42.335 --> 32:43.920
I feel nothing when I cut them down.

32:51.052 --> 32:52.596
So, have you lost your heart?

33:07.110 --> 33:08.445
Honestly...

33:14.951 --> 33:16.995
I didn't want to meet you like this.

33:18.413 --> 33:19.456
Don't.

33:23.919 --> 33:25.754
I guess we have no choice, Izo.

33:26.463 --> 33:28.006
Don't, Toshizo.

33:32.093 --> 33:33.762
At least, I'll be the one to cut you down.

33:39.017 --> 33:40.393
I am Mibu Roshigumi Vice-Commander...

33:42.437 --> 33:43.688
Hijikata Toshizo.

33:46.233 --> 33:47.359
Here I come!

33:57.369 --> 34:01.373
I am Izo, the Manslayer.

34:01.498 --> 34:03.416
No, you aren't.

34:30.735 --> 34:32.112
Damn, you're strong.

34:34.614 --> 34:35.864
Interesting.

34:39.327 --> 34:41.246
You're still Izo, through and through.

34:51.380 --> 34:52.757
From here on

34:54.134 --> 34:56.094
I'm just Hijikata Toshizo.

35:01.933 --> 35:04.227
You said it yourself, Izo.

35:04.352 --> 35:07.063
"With wooden swords, we can fight
as many times as we want."

35:07.731 --> 35:09.232
But I guess that's not an option now!

35:13.737 --> 35:17.949
This is a fight to the death.
Our first and last duel.

35:24.623 --> 35:28.460
Izo, after this,
we can never do this again.

35:29.210 --> 35:31.588
There's no greater honor
than to fall by your blade.

35:32.631 --> 35:35.425
I know you feel the same. Izo!

35:52.609 --> 35:54.277
Damn, that hurts!

35:55.070 --> 35:57.364
Hey! How does that feel?
Tell me, does a scarecrow bleed?

35:59.366 --> 36:01.284
What you just cut wasn't
a scarecrow, was it?

36:02.077 --> 36:05.580
See? You feel pain, don't you?

36:08.625 --> 36:10.585
And the man I'm fighting isn't
a scarecrow either.

36:12.087 --> 36:15.715
I'm fighting you! Okada Izo!

36:28.103 --> 36:31.940
Hey, what was it we were striving for

36:33.650 --> 36:34.651
Izo?

36:52.669 --> 36:55.505
To become the strongest man alive,
wasn't it?

37:33.877 --> 37:35.962
I don't need something like this

37:38.965 --> 37:40.592
to duel you, Toshizo.

38:01.237 --> 38:04.741
That's more like it, Izo.

38:09.913 --> 38:11.372
All right.

38:15.668 --> 38:16.753
You can continue

38:18.463 --> 38:19.798
to fight with those.

38:26.971 --> 38:28.014
Boss.

38:51.621 --> 38:52.789
Toshizo.

38:54.791 --> 38:55.959
Bring it on!

38:59.963 --> 39:01.089
Yeah!

40:06.237 --> 40:07.488
I am Okada Izo!

40:08.031 --> 40:13.536
The strongest man in all of Japan!

40:14.996 --> 40:19.459
I'm the greatest samurai in all of Japan!

40:30.929 --> 40:33.473
- I won!
- I won!

40:45.151 --> 40:46.819
Looks like another draw.

40:47.904 --> 40:48.905
Toshizo...

40:53.076 --> 40:54.160
Man...

40:56.829 --> 40:58.831
That was a damn good time.

41:13.012 --> 41:15.098
Hey, Toshizo.

41:18.393 --> 41:19.477
Someday...

41:21.312 --> 41:22.480
Someday...

41:26.192 --> 41:27.527
we'll do this again.

41:30.947 --> 41:32.824
No matter how much I boast of my strength

41:32.949 --> 41:34.867
don't you dare run away next time.

41:49.966 --> 41:52.010
What's wrong with you, Toshizo?

41:53.928 --> 41:55.096
You're one to talk.

41:58.016 --> 42:02.395
No matter where you hide,
no matter where you run

42:03.604 --> 42:08.234
I'll find you
and beat the hell out of you!

42:15.324 --> 42:16.451
Toshizo.

42:17.952 --> 42:21.330
You're a real weirdo.

42:22.999 --> 42:28.921
We just made this incredible promise.
So why are you crying?

42:30.339 --> 42:31.758
Shut up!

42:33.468 --> 42:35.344
You're the one who's crying!

42:38.389 --> 42:39.432
What?

42:40.516 --> 42:42.018
But why?

42:54.322 --> 42:55.531
It's a promise, then.

43:00.995 --> 43:02.080
I promise.

43:27.021 --> 43:29.982
After that, Okada Izo was captured in Kyo

43:31.109 --> 43:32.944
and extradited to the Tosa Domain.

43:34.821 --> 43:40.952
He was imprisoned with Takechi Hanpeita
and the rest of the Tosa Loyalist Party.

43:44.539 --> 43:45.623
Hey...

43:47.834 --> 43:49.001
You...

43:52.130 --> 43:54.006
A wooden sword.

43:55.341 --> 43:57.009
Can you lend one to me?

44:00.471 --> 44:01.806
A wooden sword?

44:02.974 --> 44:05.059
What are you going to do with that?

44:07.728 --> 44:09.063
Toshizo

44:10.731 --> 44:12.108
is waiting for me.

44:19.699 --> 44:21.159
Toshizo

44:22.869 --> 44:24.120
is getting stronger

44:27.248 --> 44:29.041
and waiting for me.

45:05.786 --> 45:08.539
Then, on July 3, 1865

45:08.664 --> 45:14.086
Okada Izo was executed by beheading.

45:14.879 --> 45:17.006
They say he was swinging that wooden sword

45:17.131 --> 45:19.217
right up to his final moment.

45:29.143 --> 45:30.770
I can't believe it.

45:31.479 --> 45:33.564
The man they called "Izo the Manslayer"...

45:35.149 --> 45:37.652
Once in Edo and once in Kyo.

45:38.236 --> 45:42.698
To think that was all it took
to forge such a powerful bond.

45:45.326 --> 45:49.163
That's what it means to cross swords
with your life on the line.

45:50.206 --> 45:53.125
Social status and personal beliefs
don't matter.

45:54.585 --> 45:58.339
You just throw pure strength
at one another.

46:00.758 --> 46:04.553
A battle like that is
every samurai's dream.

46:06.806 --> 46:09.392
I'm envious of a bond like that.

46:10.226 --> 46:11.394
It may

46:13.020 --> 46:15.523
have been the last dream
either of them ever had.

46:17.525 --> 46:19.151
Their last dream?

46:22.321 --> 46:23.614
Sadly...

46:25.324 --> 46:27.785
after that, the battles we fought

46:30.037 --> 46:33.249
were a far cry from any such dream.

46:41.632 --> 46:44.260
Hey, Hijikata, what are you doing?

46:45.261 --> 46:46.304
The corps regulations.

46:47.263 --> 46:49.265
To keep the riffraff in line.

47:03.029 --> 47:05.197
That's just like you, Toshi. I love it.

47:05.364 --> 47:06.866
- You really think so?
- Yeah.

47:08.617 --> 47:10.536
We'll fight and clash

47:10.661 --> 47:12.038
to keep the corps' rules in place.

47:12.204 --> 47:14.832
- "The fight is on!"
- Make sure everyone stays in line.

47:18.336 --> 47:20.087
You didn't have to tear it up, Soji!

47:20.212 --> 47:21.714
I'm impressed you
wrote something so idiotic.

47:21.839 --> 47:23.215
In fact, it's almost brilliant.

47:24.633 --> 47:25.676
Kondo.

47:30.306 --> 47:32.308
Never mind Hijikata's scribbles.

47:33.184 --> 47:34.477
Use this.

47:36.395 --> 47:38.189
Who does he think he is?

47:38.314 --> 47:40.649
Now, now. Let's see what you've got.

47:45.363 --> 47:47.031
"The Corps Code."

47:50.159 --> 47:53.871
"One. Do not stray
from the Way of the samurai.

47:54.413 --> 47:58.542
One. Desertion of the corps is forbidden.

47:59.377 --> 48:03.297
One. You are forbidden
to raise money without authorization.

48:03.422 --> 48:07.885
One. You are forbidden
to involve yourself in litigation.

48:08.386 --> 48:12.890
One. Do not engage in personal fights.

48:15.434 --> 48:17.061
Anyone who violates these articles

48:20.773 --> 48:21.816
must commit seppuku."

48:23.401 --> 48:25.569
That's pretty harsh, isn't it?

48:25.694 --> 48:29.073
Okita, this is no time
for such naive talk.

48:30.032 --> 48:32.326
This isn't Shieikan anymore.

48:33.202 --> 48:35.871
To restore order to the chaos in Kyo

48:36.330 --> 48:38.332
the unity of our corps
is absolutely essential.

48:39.417 --> 48:42.002
But still, seppuku seems extreme.

48:42.128 --> 48:43.254
Yamanami.

48:44.755 --> 48:45.840
What is it?

48:45.965 --> 48:47.466
Are you against it, too?

48:49.260 --> 48:50.594
Add two more rules.

48:58.185 --> 48:59.395
"One.

49:00.729 --> 49:02.773
Draw your sword and fight
until you or your opponent has fallen.

49:04.859 --> 49:05.901
One.

49:07.445 --> 49:08.696
If you fail to kill
and take a wound to your back

49:08.821 --> 49:10.030
it is seppuku."

49:11.532 --> 49:12.825
That means...

49:14.285 --> 49:15.911
once you draw your sword, you must win.

49:16.036 --> 49:17.121
Soji.

49:19.081 --> 49:20.249
This is about resolve.

49:23.961 --> 49:25.713
Without this level of resolve

49:28.048 --> 49:29.675
you can't protect the things that matter.

49:36.182 --> 49:37.391
I...

49:41.520 --> 49:43.439
don't want to lose any more comrades.

49:47.902 --> 49:48.944
That's true.

49:51.572 --> 49:53.449
The stricter these rules are

49:54.533 --> 49:57.703
the more justification we'll have to keep

49:57.828 --> 49:59.747
Serizawa's rogue faction in check.

50:00.498 --> 50:01.790
A just cause.

50:01.916 --> 50:02.958
Yes.

50:03.501 --> 50:05.753
At the very least,
it should slow them down.

50:07.171 --> 50:08.547
- Is it good?
- Yes.

50:09.590 --> 50:11.258
The Corps Code?

50:13.636 --> 50:17.806
"One. Do not stray
from the Way of the samurai.

50:18.182 --> 50:22.436
One. Desertion of the corps is forbidden.

50:22.561 --> 50:23.562
One. You are forbidden
to raise money without authorization."

50:23.687 --> 50:27.816
Yamazaki here can memorize anything
he sees and hears, down to every detail

50:27.942 --> 50:30.194
and is able to recall it perfectly.

50:31.779 --> 50:33.447
- A natural-born spy, huh?
- "One. You are forbidden

50:33.572 --> 50:34.615
to involve yourself in litigation.

50:35.491 --> 50:36.951
Anyone who violates these rules..."

50:37.159 --> 50:38.744
YAMAZAKI SUSUMU

50:38.869 --> 50:40.162
"...Seppuku."

50:49.630 --> 50:51.549
The stricter these rules are

50:52.174 --> 50:55.094
the more justification we'll have
to keep Serizawa's rogue faction

50:55.594 --> 50:57.346
in check.

50:58.055 --> 51:00.432
- This is obviously aimed at us.
- A just cause.

51:00.558 --> 51:01.892
Those bastards.

51:02.017 --> 51:03.269
We have to do something.

51:03.394 --> 51:05.563
I like it. The Corps Code.

51:05.688 --> 51:06.689
What?

51:06.814 --> 51:11.485
But this business about committing seppuku
for breaking it, I don't like.

51:12.111 --> 51:16.407
If we play this right,
we could use it to tighten the noose.

51:16.532 --> 51:17.616
Is that so?

51:18.158 --> 51:19.952
Hey, good work.

51:20.160 --> 51:22.663
Money... Money!

51:51.775 --> 51:54.570
"Half past six.
I'll be waiting at Shinkenji Temple."

52:02.911 --> 52:04.622
Guess who?
